  "published": "2025-12-14T01:46:45.45Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "mostlylucid.mockllmapi — Release Notes\n\n===============================================================================\nRelease 2.3.0 — 2025-12-13\n===============================================================================\n\nComplete Content Type Support - Forms, Files, Deep Paths\n\n1. Form Body Support (application/x-www-form-urlencoded)\n   - Automatic conversion of form data to JSON\n   - Single + multiple values (arrays for duplicate field names)\n   - Special character escaping (quotes, backslashes, newlines, tabs)\n   - Unicode and emoji support\n   - Manual JSON construction for .NET 10 compatibility\n\n2. File Upload Support (multipart/form-data)\n   - Memory-safe streaming: Files read through 8KB buffer and dumped\n   - Metadata extraction: filename, content type, size, bytes read\n   - Multiple files + mixed form fields in single request\n   - Large file support (tested with 100MB+)\n   - Constant O(1) memory usage regardless of file size\n\n3. Arbitrary Path Lengths\n   - Full support for deep nested paths (tested to 21 segments)\n   - Query parameters fully preserved\n   - Works with all HTTP methods + content types\n   - Perfect for RESTful API structures\n\nUsage Examples:\n  # Form submission\n  curl -X POST http://localhost:5116/api/mock/users/register \\\n    -d \"username=john&email=john@example.com\"\n\n  # File upload\n  curl -X POST http://localhost:5116/api/mock/photos/upload \\\n    -F \"title=My Photo\" -F \"image=@photo.jpg\"\n\n  # Deep path\n  curl \"http://localhost:5116/api/mock/v1/api/products/electronics/laptops\"\n\nTesting: 60 new tests (405 total, 100% pass rate)\n  - FormBodyHandlingTests.cs (12 tests) - form parsing\n  - JsonHandlingTests.cs (25 tests) - escaping + extraction\n  - V2_3_0_FeatureTests.cs (23 tests) - full integration\n\nTechnical: Manual JSON construction throughout for .NET 10 AOT compatibility\n\nDocs: TEST_SUMMARY.md, IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md, V2_3_0_TESTS.md\n\nBreaking Changes: None - fully backward compatible\n\n===============================================================================\nRelease 2.2.0 — 2025-01-14\n===============================================================================\n\nPluggable Tools & Pre-Configured APIs\n\n- HTTP/Mock tools system (MCP-compatible)\n- Pre-configured REST APIs (define once, call by name)\n- Auto-expiring context memory (15 min default)\n- Enhanced shared data extraction (recursive)\n\n===============================================================================\nRelease 2.1.0 — 2025-01-06\n===============================================================================\n\nQuality & Validation - 70+ Tests, Enhanced Chunking, Swagger Docs\n\nFull history: github.com/ScottGalloway/mostlylucid.mockllmapi",
